{"content":"## Fixed — the latch guard is now fail-closed standalone

Applied the suggested guard at the top of the `mergeStateLatch` block in `js/sm/sources/githubSource.js`:

```javascript
if (q.mergeStateLatch) {
    // Fail closed standalone: an item with NO merge-state observation
    // (pr-less issue carrier, pr carrier whose status never resolved)
    // must not sail through a latch over a listed state — an unknown
    // merge state is not CLEAN.
    if (!item.pr) return false;
    ...
}
```

This matches the documented "Fails CLOSED" contract in the comment block. Behavior of the deployed rule is unchanged (its pr-less items were already rejected by `notMergeState`), and states not listed in the latch stay inert.

Pinned with two RED-first tests in the gh-829 suite:

- `latch guard fails closed on pr-less items — issue carrier without a linked PR` — an `ai_developed`-labeled issue with no linked PR is excluded; only the issue with a linked CLEAN PR matches.
- `latch guard fails closed on pr-less items — pr carrier whose status never resolved` — a latch-only query has no `checks`/`mergeState`/`notMergeState` guard, so `queryPrs` never fetches `prStatus` and `item.pr` stays `null`; the head stays unarmed even with the latch label on its issue.

Both failed on the pre-fix engine (pr-less items passed the guard) and pass after the fix.
","path":"outputs/review_replies/thread_2.md"}

{"content":"## Fixed — harness extracted into a shared `maskedGreenHarness()`

Hoisted the duplicated wiring to module scope of `js/unit-tests/test_smGithubSource.js`, just above the gh-759 suite. The helper owns the one `providerStub` (same four stubbed methods), the `smAsync`/`githubSource` `loadModule` wiring, and the shared `pr(n, labels, …)` factory — exactly the ~50 lines that were copied.

The suites now differ only in their label fixtures: `load(tools, prs, statuses, issueLabels, issueErrors)` takes the gh-829 latch fixtures per call (omitted → every linked issue resolves label-less, the pre-gh-829 gh-759 wave shape), and both suites open with:

```javascript
var h = maskedGreenHarness();
var load = h.load;
var pr = h.pr;
```

Future gh-7xx follow-ups edit a single copy of the wiring. The full 54-test `test_smGithubSource.js` suite stays green, as does the full repo suite (2279 passed, 0 failed).
","path":"outputs/review_replies/thread_3.md"}

{"content":"## Fixed — the no-fetch contract is now pinned with a throwing stub

The `BLOCKED branch needs no latch and no issue fetch` test now overrides the default stub via `load()`'s tools merge, exactly as suggested:

```javascript
github_get_issue: function () {
    throw new Error('latch must not fetch the issue on the BLOCKED path');
}
```

The test comment was updated to explain why: `load()` always injected a label-less *returning* stub, which would happily answer a regression that consulted the issue on the BLOCKED path. With the throwing stub, the no-fetch half of the gh-757 contract fails loudly instead of passing silently; the result half (guests match — `pr-900`, `pr-901`) is unchanged and green.
